From: iOSPlus10 ios26 port
Subject: [PATCH 0003] NEGRONI machine layer: GICv3 Group 1 IRQs, start.s, SMP/PSCI, early framebuffer, CPU idle

The iOS 16 machine-layer state (xnu-8796 + slop + patches/xnu) carried to xnu-12377.121.6:
- pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c: Group 1 NS GIC setup, vtimer INTID / redistributor stride from the ADT, SPI
  register/dispatch (slop 0004, 0017, 0082; ours 0288, 0295)
- osfmk/arm64/sleh.c: timer/IPI/SPI as Group 1 IRQs, kernel-thread backtraces, MMIO try accessors with the
  FnV SEA case (slop 0004, 0084, 0085, 0086; ours 0297). 12377 also matches the expected-fault PC.
- osfmk/arm64/start.s: MPIDR Aff1 core numbers, PSCI CPU_ON entry negroni_secondary_entry (EL2 or EL1),
  early white band, splash framebuffer block, no SCTLR equality check (slop 0010, 0065, 0078)
- osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c: cpus=N clamp, cluster ids from Aff1, no CNTP_CTL write under Gunyah (slop 0083)
- osfmk/arm64/cpu.c: PoC cleans of the reset data for PSCI secondaries
- osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c, negroni_early.[ch]: early framebuffer marks across the TTBR switch
- osfmk/arm64/negroni_cpuidle.c (ours 0288/0382/0383): PSCI idle; the RPMh hooks are weak until
  bsd/dev/negroni_rpmh.c is ported
- arm_init.c, model_dep.c, caches_asm.s (clean_mmu_dcache label), protos.h (SERIAL_NEGRONI_FBCON = 0x10:
  12377 merged PI3/VMAPPLE into SERIAL_PL011_UART = 0x4)
Not needed on 12377: 0363/0378 boot-line 1024 (12377 BOOT_LINE_LENGTH is already 1024), kpc.c stub (12377 has kpc.c).

