diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/negroni_cpuidle.c b/osfmk/arm64/negroni_cpuidle.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..35256c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/negroni_cpuidle.c
@@ -0,0 +1,797 @@
+/*
+ * NEGRONI (SM8450) CPU idle states, patch 0288.
+ *
+ * Before 0288 an idle core ran XNU's cpu_idle() -> WFI (osfmk/arm64/cpu.c): clock gating only, the
+ * core and its L1/L2 stay powered. This file adds the PSCI CPU_SUSPEND states of the phone's device
+ * tree (out/live.dts:733-775, idle-states; cpus at 512-673; psci node at 1217-1272):
+ *
+ *   silver-c4 "rail-pc"  cpus 0-3   param 0x40000004  entry 800 us  exit  750 us  residency  4090 us  local-timer-stop
+ *   gold-c4   "rail-pc"  cpus 4-7   param 0x40000004  entry 600 us  exit 1550 us  residency  4791 us  local-timer-stop
+ *   cluster-d4 "l3-off"  (cluster)  param 0x41000044  entry 1050 us exit 2500 us  residency  5309 us
+ *   cluster-e3 "llcc-off"(cluster)  param 0x4100c344  entry 2700 us exit 3500 us  residency 13959 us
+ *
+ * The params use the PSCI extended StateID format (bit 30 = power-down, StateID in bits 27:0); the
+ * cluster states are domain-idle-states of the psci cluster-pd (Linux cpuidle-psci-domain.c composes
+ * them in OS-initiated mode). Linux starts PSCI in platform-coordinated mode (drivers/firmware/psci/
+ * psci.c:578-592, psci_1_0_init "Default to PC mode") and moves to OSI only for the hierarchical
+ * domains; this file stays in PC mode: each core asks for its own state, and with negronicpuidle=2 for a
+ * cluster state, which the firmware enters only when every core of the cluster asked for it.
+ *
+ * Boot-arg negronicpuidle (default 0 = WFI only, as before):
+ *   1  a core whose next timer deadline is at least the state's residency away powers down (rail-pc)
+ *   2  + the cluster states (l3-off at >= 5309 us, llcc-off at >= 13959 us)
+ * negronicpuidle_mask (default 0xff: the cores that may power down), negronicpuidle_bcast (default 1).
+ *
+ * Power-down loses the core's state. Entry point = negroni_secondary_entry (start.s, the PSCI CPU_ON
+ * entry), which goes to the reset vector; cpu_machine_idle_init already set every core's reset
+ * handler to resume_idle_cpu, so the core comes back through start_cpu -> arm_init_idle_cpu ->
+ * cpu_idle_exit(TRUE) (XNU's own deep-idle path), where negroni_cpuidle_resume() runs first: the GIC
+ * CPU interface again (PE_init_cpu = pe_init_fiq, as Linux's gic_cpu_pm_notifier -> gic_cpu_sys_reg_init)
+ * and the virtual timer's deadline again (setPop; arm_init_idle_cpu already re-enabled CNTV_CTL and
+ * CNTKCTL). A CPU_SUSPEND that returns did not power down: cpu_idle goes on as after a WFI.
+ *
+ * "local-timer-stop": the core's own timer does not run while it is down. Linux uses a broadcast timer
+ * (the memory-mapped timer, out/live.dts:1344-1357 timer@17420000 "arm,armv7-timer-mem", frame 0 at
+ * 0x17421000, physical-timer SPI 8 = INTID 40). Here the same: the earliest wake time of the cores that
+ * are down is programmed into frame 0's CNTP_CVAL (exit latency earlier), its SPI is routed to that
+ * core, and the interrupt handler (sleh.c NEGRONI path) sends an IPI to every core whose time came.
+ * [I] Under the Gunyah hypervisor the virtual timer of a suspended vCPU may keep working; the broadcast
+ * is then only a second wake source. negronicpuidle_bcast=0 turns it off (only for tests).
+ *
+ * A simple guard against short sleeps (qcom-lpm.c has a history predictor): three power-downs in a row
+ * shorter than the residency -> the next 8 idles of that core are WFI.
+ * Log: "NEGRONI CPUIDLE: ..." at start, then every 60 s one line per core and state:
+ * "NEGRONI CPUIDLE: cpuN state S param 0x... entered N times: ...".
+ *
+ * Patch 0383 (cluster states as Linux, RPMh sleep sets, sleep statistics):
+ * - Gunyah (the hypervisor) implements PSCI for the HLOS VM (quic/gunyah-hypervisor hyp/vm/psci_osi): FEATURES
+ *   (CPU_SUSPEND) = 3 for the HLOS (OSI + extended StateID), the VM starts in PC mode, a vCPU in WFI stays "active"
+ *   for the aggregation, so the physical core only clock-gates (psci_osi_handle_idle_yield: no suspend while an
+ *   affine vCPU is active). Only CPU_SUSPEND lets Gunyah power the core, the cluster (L3) or the APSS down.
+ * - negronicpuidle=3: OS-initiated mode, as Linux cpuidle-psci-domain (psci_pd_init_topology -> psci_set_osi_mode):
+ *   SET_SUSPEND_MODE(OSI) at start (Gunyah allows it while every other vCPU is active = here, before ci_ready), then
+ *   the last core (every other core inside CPU_SUSPEND) passes the cluster param when the earliest deadline of all
+ *   cores is at least the cluster residency away (the genpd governor's next wakeup); the others pass the core param.
+ *   Gunyah answers DENIED when its view differs (osi_mode_suspend_state_validation_at_level): counted, then 4 idles
+ *   core-only. If SET_SUSPEND_MODE fails, level 3 works as level 2 (PC).
+ * - Before any cluster param: negroni_rpmh_sleep_ready() (bsd/dev/negroni_rpmh.c) must say the RPMh DRV is idle and
+ *   its SLEEP/WAKE sets are current (Linux rpmh_rsc_pd_cb at the cluster PRE_OFF); else the core param.
+ * - llcc-off (cluster-e3, the state with the APSS RSC sleep) only with negronicpuidle_llcc=1 (default 0).
+ * - Sleep statistics, read-only (negronicpuidle_stats, default 7 at level >= 1, 0 at level 0): bit 0 the AOP
+ *   rpmh-sleep-stats records (live.dts soc-sleep-stats@c3f0000, Linux soc_sleep_stats.c rpmh_data: base = 0xc3f0000 |
+ *   [0xc3f0004], 3 records of 32 bytes: name, count, last entered, last exited, accumulated 19.2 MHz ticks), bit 1 the
+ *   DDR stats (base = 0xc3f0000 | [0xc3f001c], magic 0xa1157a75), bit 2 the CPUSS LPM counters (live.dts
+ *   cpuss-sleep-stats apss_seq_mem_base 0x178c0000, qcom_cpuss_sleep_stats.c v1 offsets: C4 count 0x80d8 + 8n,
+ *   cluster D4 count at n = 8, C4/D4 residency 0xc0d0 + 8n). One line each per 60 s with the change.
+ */
+#include <pexpert/arm64/board_config.h>
+
+#if defined(NEGRONI)
+#include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <kern/clock.h>
